<EVALUATION_CRITERIA>

## SIMPLE Task Characteristics
- Single well-defined task
- Clear, unambiguous requirements
- Can be executed in one session (<1 hour of focused work)
- No external dependencies beyond standard libraries
- Straightforward implementation using known patterns
- Single domain/technology
- Standard operations (CRUD, refactoring, bug fixes)

## COMPLEX Task Characteristics
- Multiple distinct domains/technologies (frontend + backend + database)
- Requires research or exploration before execution
- Ambiguous or underspecified requirements
- Multiple subtasks with potential dependencies
- Needs architectural or design decisions
- Coordinates multiple systems/services
- Estimated >1 hour of focused work
- Novel problem without established solution patterns

</EVALUATION_CRITERIA>

<EXAMPLES>

### SIMPLE Examples
- "Write a Python function to calculate Fibonacci numbers"
- "Add input validation to the UserService.create_user method"
- "Refactor the User model to use properties instead of direct attributes"
- "Fix bug where logout doesn't clear session cookie"
- "Research BeautifulSoup library documentation"

### COMPLEX Examples
- "Build a web scraper for news articles" (research + implementation + testing + deployment)
- "Implement user authentication system" (database schema + API + security + sessions)
- "Create a recommendation engine" (data collection + algorithm + training + deployment)
- "Add real-time notifications" (WebSocket + event system + frontend integration)
- "Migrate from REST API to GraphQL" (schema design + server setup + client updates)

</EXAMPLES>

<SUCCESS_CRITERIA>
- Make a clear binary decision: SIMPLE or COMPLEX
- Provide specific reasoning citing task characteristics
- Be decisive and confident in your classification
</SUCCESS_CRITERIA>
